      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Dead-Letter Implementation**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the implementation for a `dead_letter.py` file. I'm leaning toward using AWS SQS as the external provider, making the integration concrete. This ensures a reliable destination for failed messages and allows for easier identification within the code.\n\n\n**Implementing Dead-Letter Handling**\n\nI've made progress by creating the `dead_letter.py` file with code that leverages the `boto3` library for AWS SQS. The code now includes a dedicated function for sending messages to a dead-letter queue and a placeholder for the queue URL, establishing the external provider.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861364922,
          "start": 1789861362757
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc0cfc45001OgaqCU8Fra4WVZ",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc0cf7d9001OCNtgEdo3fNwZE",
      "session_id": "ses_f43f30834fferIcybwsAuZsV6B",
      "time_created": 1789861362757,
      "time_updated": 1789861364923
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "gUj4GE5muqiKxVNY",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef send_to_dead_letter_queue(message_body, queue_url=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sends a failed message to an AWS SQS dead-letter queue.\n\n    Args:\n        message_body (str): The content of the failed message.\n        queue_url (str, optional): The URL of the dead-letter queue.\n                                   If not provided, it tries to read from DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL env var.\n    \"\"\"\n    if queue_url is None:\n        queue_url = os.environ.get(\"DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\")\n\n    if not queue_url:\n        print(\"Error: Dead-letter queue URL not provided and DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL environment variable is not set.\")\n        return\n\n    try:\n        sqs = boto3.client(\"sqs\")\n        response = sqs.send_message(\n            QueueUrl=queue_url,\n            MessageBody=message_body\n        )\n        print(f\"Message sent to dead-letter queue: {response['MessageId']}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error sending message to dead-letter queue: {e}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Set the environment variable before running, or pass the queue_url directly\n    # os.environ[\"DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\"] = \"YOUR_DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\"\n    failed_message = \"This is a message that failed processing.\"\n    send_to_dead_letter_queue(failed_message, \"https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/123456789012/MyDeadLetterQueue\") # Replace with your actual SQS Dead Letter Queue URL\n",
            "filePath": "dead_letter.py"
          },
