    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Pub/Sub Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Pub/Sub as the external provider for the `consume_event.py` script, as it's a good choice for managed subscriptions. Now, I'll focus on how to best integrate the Pub/Sub client library into this Python file.\n\n\n**Defining Pub/Sub Script**\n\nI'm now going to focus on creating the `consume_event.py` file with the Pub/Sub client library. I've decided on Google Cloud Pub/Sub, so I'll include the necessary library imports and placeholder values for the project and subscription IDs. The script will need to incorporate the `subscriber.subscribe` functionality to consume a single message.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861359408,
          "start": 1789861357022
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc0ce5de001Zhfkywf7Q7bWFW",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc0ce139001okmma9O6K2YZ0h",
      "session_id": "ses_f43f31ed8ffefB0D85DF93Q5Is",
      "time_created": 1789861357022,
      "time_updated": 1789861359409
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "4i4BwjDwokvS8v5h",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import pubsub_v1\nimport os\n\n# Set your Google Cloud Project ID and Subscription ID\n# Replace with your actual project ID and subscription ID\nproject_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT\")\nsubscription_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID\")\n\nif not project_id or not subscription_id:\n    print(\"Please set the GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT and GOOGLE_CLOUD_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID environment variables.\")\n    exit()\n\nsubscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()\n# The `subscription_path` converts the project ID and subscription ID into a properly formatted string\nsubscription_path = subscriber.subscription_path(project_id, subscription_id)\n\ndef consume_message(timeout=5.0):\n    \"\"\"Consumes one message from a Pub/Sub subscription.\"\"\"\n\n    def callback(message):\n        print(f\"Received message: {message.data.decode('utf-8')}\")\n        message.ack()\n\n    streaming_pull_future = subscriber.subscribe(subscription_path, callback=callback)\n    print(f\"Listening for messages on {subscription_path}...\")\n\n    try:\n        # Blocks the current thread until the timeout is reached or the subscriber is stopped\n        streaming_pull_future.result(timeout=timeout)\n    except TimeoutError:\n        print(\"No messages received within the timeout period.\")\n        streaming_pull_future.cancel()\n        streaming_pull_future.result()\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n        streaming_pull_future.cancel()\n        streaming_pull_future.result()\n    finally:\n        subscriber.api.transport.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    consume_message()\n",
            "filePath": "consume_event.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
